From: shphadnis <134159681+shphadnis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 16:59:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] spectro: fedora virt-v2v image target and nbdkit fix

Re-derived on upstream v2.12.1 (was 51f4b6625/8053d5635 PR #29, and
59eb19619 + eb91d63cd/bdd3b674b PR #46 on the 2.9.2 line).

Adds build-virt-v2v-fedora-image / push-virt-v2v-fedora-image and bumps
the Fedora base 41 -> 43 with virtio-win 1.9.45-1.el10, which is the
nbdkit fix the VMO appliance needs.

Deliberately NOT carried from the 2.9.2 version:
  - builder image is left as upstream's centos:stream9 + libvirt-devel.
    The 2.9.2 fork used ubi9/go-toolset, which predates the libvirt cgo
    dependency in pkg/virt-v2v/conversion and can no longer build it.
  - LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND is left as upstream's libvirt:qemu:///session.
    v2.12.1 already fixes RHEL-104684/105490/105529 (direct backend for
    the appliance build, qemu cache dir, catatonit as PID 1). Our
    conversion pod still sets LIBGUESTFS_BACKEND=direct at runtime, which
    overrides the image default where we need it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Makefile                                     | 7 +++++++
 build/virt-v2v/Containerfile-upstream-fedora | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -358,6 +358,13 @@ push-virt-v2v-xfs-image: build-virt-v2v-xfs-image
 		$(CONTAINER_CMD) push $(VIRT_V2V_IMAGE_RHEL9)$(PLATFORM_SUFFIX); \
 	fi
 
+build-virt-v2v-fedora-image: check_container_runtime
+	$(eval VIRT_V2V_IMAGE=$(REGISTRY)/$(REGISTRY_ORG)/forklift-virt-v2v:$(REGISTRY_TAG))
+	$(CONTAINER_CMD) build $(PLATFORM_FLAG) -t $(VIRT_V2V_IMAGE) -f build/virt-v2v/Containerfile-upstream-fedora .
+
+push-virt-v2v-fedora-image: build-virt-v2v-fedora-image
+	$(CONTAINER_CMD) push $(VIRT_V2V_IMAGE)
+
 build-operator-bundle-image: check_container_runtime
 	$(CONTAINER_CMD) build $(PLATFORM_FLAG) $(BUILD_LABEL_ARGS) \
 		-t $(OPERATOR_BUNDLE_IMAGE)$(PLATFORM_SUFFIX) \
diff --git a/build/virt-v2v/Containerfile-upstream-fedora b/build/virt-v2v/Containerfile-upstream-fedora
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/build/virt-v2v/Containerfile-upstream-fedora
+++ b/build/virt-v2v/Containerfile-upstream-fedora
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@ RUN go build -buildvcs=false -ldflags="-w -s" -o virt-v2v-wrapper ./cmd/virt-v2v
 RUN go build -buildvcs=false -ldflags="-w -s" -o forklift-wait-for-reboot github.com/kubev2v/forklift/cmd/forklift-wait-for-reboot
 
 # Main container
-FROM quay.io/fedora/fedora:41
+FROM quay.io/fedora/fedora:43
 RUN rm /etc/pki/tls/fips_local.cnf && \
     echo -e '[fips_sect]\ntls1-prf-ems-check = 0\nactivate = 1' > /etc/pki/tls/fips_local.cnf && \
     sed -i '/^\\[ crypto_policy \\]/a Options=RHNoEnforceEMSinFIPS' /etc/pki/tls/openssl.cnf
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@ RUN mkdir /disks && \
         virt-v2v && \
     dnf clean all
 
-RUN dnf install -y https://kojihub.stream.centos.org/kojifiles/packages/virtio-win/1.9.40/1.el9/noarch/virtio-win-1.9.40-1.el9.noarch.rpm
+RUN dnf install -y https://kojihub.stream.centos.org/kojifiles/packages/virtio-win/1.9.45/1.el10/noarch/virtio-win-1.9.45-1.el10.noarch.rpm
 
 
 # Missing `libguestfs-winsupport` in the Fedora packages, this is not needed for Fedora as the v2v uses ntfs-3g
